<edge source="russia_ukraine_warfare::energy_infra_attack_rate" target="brics_economic_realignme::state_control_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">A rise in attacks on energy and transport infrastructure prompts governments to impose emergency regulatory controls, tighter licensing, asset seizures and cybersecurity restrictions to secure critical systems and maintain supply, increasing overall state control intensity.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_warfare</data>
  <data key="d40">brics_economic_realignme</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_warfare::energy_infra_attack_rate" target="global_rate_market_shock::financial_conditions_ind" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Increased attacks on energy and transport infrastructure raise market volatility, disrupt commodity flows and trade, and widen credit and funding spreads, reducing liquidity and thus tightening overall financial conditions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_warfare</data>
  <data key="d40">global_rate_market_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_warfare::energy_infra_attack_rate" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::regulatory_pressure" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Visible attacks on energy and transport infrastructure that employ remotely guided or autonomous systems increase political pressure and produce concrete legislative proposals to tighten oversight of dual‑use AI and autonomy technologies.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_warfare</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
