<edge source="russia_ukraine_warfare::sanctions_severity" target="brics_economic_realignme::external_financial_links" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">More severe and broader sanctions (banking, SWIFT access, asset freezes) cause foreign correspondent banks, custodians and investors to sever or limit links with targeted counterparties and jurisdictions, directly reducing the strength of external financial connections.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_warfare</data>
  <data key="d40">brics_economic_realignme</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_warfare::sanctions_severity" target="global_rate_market_shock::policy_rate_expectations" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Expansion and intensification of sanctions increase import costs and inflationary pressures, leading markets to revise up the expected path and timing of monetary tightening by central banks.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_warfare</data>
  <data key="d40">global_rate_market_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_warfare::sanctions_severity" target="red_sea_hormuz_crisis::cargo_rerouting_volume" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Tightening and broadening of sanctions on Russian energy and shipping increases legal, compliance and seizure risk for counterparties, causing traders and carriers to reroute, delay, or withhold cargoes that would otherwise transit Red Sea/Hormuz corridors.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_warfare</data>
  <data key="d40">red_sea_hormuz_crisis</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_warfare::sanctions_severity" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::ai_investment_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Escalating sanctions on Russia prompt broader export controls and investor de‑risking, causing capital to be reallocated away from sanction‑exposed markets into domestic and allied AI firms and infrastructure.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_warfare</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
