  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">Sharp rises in crude spot prices driven by Red Sea/Hormuz disruptions increase domestic energy costs and inflationary pressure in sanctioning countries, reducing political tolerance for additional or harsher sanctions on Russia and thus lowering aggregate sanctions severity.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
