<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::model_deployment_rate" target="brics_economic_realignme::state_control_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Faster, wider deployment of advanced models increases incidents of data leakage, misuse and rapid diffusion of sensitive capabilities, triggering BRICS regulators to impose broader administrative controls and tighter oversight on platforms and data flows.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">brics_economic_realignme</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::model_deployment_rate" target="red_sea_hormuz_crisis::cargo_rerouting_volume" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Rapid corporate deployment of powerful open models lowers the technical barrier for GPS/AIS spoofing, automated coordination of small-boat/drone harassment and real-time misinformation campaigns, prompting shippers and traders to reroute or withhold vulnerable oil cargoes.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">red_sea_hormuz_crisis</data>
</edge>
